WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.977
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:09.362
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:14.659
Unit three: My Community. In this unit, you will suggest ways to help your community.

4
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.419
Neighbor.

5
00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:19.327
Neighbor means a person who lives near you.

6
00:00:19.627 --> 00:00:21.430
Our neighbor gives us mangoes.

7
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.329
Your turn. Say: Neighbor.

8
00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:27.810
Neighbor.

9
00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:29.771
Cooperate.

10
00:00:30.471 --> 00:00:32.750
Cooperate means to work together with others.

11
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.676
If we cooperate, we can finish quickly.

12
00:00:36.376 --> 00:00:39.214
Your turn. Say: Cooperate.

13
00:00:41.914 --> 00:00:42.927
Cooperate.

14
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:44.906
Volunteer.

15
00:00:45.606 --> 00:00:48.476
Volunteer means a person who helps without being paid.

16
00:00:48.776 --> 00:00:50.997
Volunteers teach English in my village.

17
00:00:51.697 --> 00:00:54.419
Your turn. Say: Volunteer.

18
00:00:57.119 --> 00:00:58.143
Volunteer.

19
00:00:59.150 --> 00:00:59.954
Support.

20
00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:03.025
Support means to help a person or a group.

21
00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:05.046
We support the local school.

22
00:01:05.746 --> 00:01:08.015
Your turn. Say: Support.

23
00:01:10.715 --> 00:01:11.646
Support.

24
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.477
Clean up.

25
00:01:14.177 --> 00:01:16.780
Clean up means to make a place clean and tidy.

26
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.975
Let's clean up the park on Saturday.

27
00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:22.432
Your turn. Say: Clean up.

28
00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:26.029
Clean up.

29
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:27.890
Together.

30
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.183
Together means with each other.

31
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:31.902
We can do more together.

32
00:01:32.602 --> 00:01:34.918
Your turn. Say: Together.

33
00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:38.515
Together.

34
00:01:39.517 --> 00:01:40.344
Charity.

35
00:01:41.044 --> 00:01:43.821
Charity means a group that helps people in need.

36
00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:46.167
This charity gives books to children.

37
00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:49.531
Your turn. Say: Charity.

38
00:01:52.231 --> 00:01:53.093
Charity.

39
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:54.968
Donate.

40
00:01:55.668 --> 00:01:58.411
Donate means to give money or things to help others.

41
00:01:58.711 --> 00:02:00.664
We donate old clothes every year.

42
00:02:01.364 --> 00:02:03.552
Your turn. Say: Donate.

43
00:02:06.252 --> 00:02:07.207
Donate.

44
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.032
Elderly.

45
00:02:09.732 --> 00:02:11.697
Elderly means old (a polite word).

46
00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:14.170
We help elderly people cross the road.

47
00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.105
Your turn. Say: Elderly.

48
00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:20.841
Elderly.

49
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:22.874
Disability.

50
00:02:23.574 --> 00:02:26.828
Disability means a condition that makes some activities difficult.

51
00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:30.044
Our school has a ramp for students with a disability.

52
00:02:30.744 --> 00:02:33.850
Your turn. Say: Disability.

53
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.667
Disability.

54
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:39.882
Inclusive.

55
00:02:40.582 --> 00:02:44.265
Inclusive means welcoming everyone, so no one is left out.

56
00:02:44.565 --> 00:02:47.426
Our club is inclusive. Everyone can join.

57
00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.395
Your turn. Say: Inclusive.

58
00:02:53.095 --> 00:02:54.282
Inclusive.

59
00:02:55.283 --> 00:02:56.493
Neighborhood watch.

60
00:02:57.193 --> 00:03:00.609
Neighborhood watch means a group of neighbors who keep the area safe.

61
00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:03.141
The neighborhood watch walks around at night.

62
00:03:03.841 --> 00:03:06.702
Your turn. Say: Neighborhood watch.

63
00:03:09.402 --> 00:03:10.752
Neighborhood watch.

64
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.750
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.885
Sreypich, how can we help our community?

66
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:20.473
Let's clean up the market street on Sunday!

67
00:03:21.783 --> 00:03:24.157
Great idea. What else should we do?

68
00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.856
We should donate books to the village library.

69
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.417
And how can we help elderly neighbors?

70
00:03:32.717 --> 00:03:35.099
We should visit them and carry their shopping.

71
00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:38.685
Grammar focus: let's and we should.

72
00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:42.043
Let's clean up the park. We should help our neighbors.

73
00:03:42.343 --> 00:03:46.075
Use 'Let's' for an idea for now. Use 'We should' to give advice.

74
00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:49.689
Now read and listen. A Better Neighborhood.

75
00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:52.337
My neighborhood is friendly and inclusive.

76
00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.555
Every month, volunteers clean up the streets together.

77
00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.546
Some families donate rice to a local charity.

78
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.080
Young people help elderly neighbors with their shopping.

79
00:04:06.383 --> 00:04:09.741
When we cooperate, our community becomes a better place.

80
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.447
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:13.747 --> 00:04:15.874
blank clean up the park on Saturday!

82
00:04:16.174 --> 00:04:19.561
A, Let's. B, Let. C, Lets to.

83
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.909
The answer is A: Let's.

84
00:04:27.417 --> 00:04:30.032
A person who helps without being paid is a blank.

85
00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:34.322
A, volunteer. B, neighbor. C, charity.

86
00:04:38.317 --> 00:04:40.827
The answer is A: volunteer.

87
00:04:42.317 --> 00:04:44.804
To give money or things to help others is to blank.

88
00:04:45.104 --> 00:04:48.142
A, donate. B, gather. C, decorate.

89
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.208
The answer is A: donate.

90
00:04:55.717 --> 00:04:58.799
Now it's your turn to speak. How can you help your community?

91
00:05:04.099 --> 00:05:09.270
Let's clean up the park together! We should also donate books and help elderly neighbors.

92
00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.338
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:16.303
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and let's and we should.

94
00:05:16.603 --> 00:05:20.370
Today's value is helping others. Give your time to help people in need.

95
00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.136
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

96
00:05:23.436 --> 00:05:26.147
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

